  "finite_identity_tex": "\\begin{gathered}c_n=\\int_n^{n+1}\\frac{(t-n)(1-\\log t)}{t^2}dt=\\frac{\\log(n+1)}{n+1}-\\frac{\\log^2(n+1)-\\log^2n}{2},\\\\\\sum_{n=1}^{N}c_n=\\sum_{k=2}^{N+1}\\frac{\\log k}{k}-\\frac{\\log^2(N+1)}2=s_{N+1}.\\end{gathered}",
  "derivative_chain_tex": "\\begin{gathered}T(s)=\\sum_{n\\ge1}\\int_n^{n+1}(t-n)t^{-s-1}dt,\\\\\\gamma_1=T(1)+T^\\prime(1),\\qquad R(h)=1-(1+h)T(1+h)\\quad(h\\ge0),\\\\R^\\prime(0)=-T(1)-T^\\prime(1)=-\\gamma_1.\\end{gathered}",
  "domains": "Finite identityN≥0,n≥1. Uniform derivative bound for actual T-series on s>3/4; identification on s≥1. R(h) is the real part of the entire regular zeta at1+h, independently differentiable. Equality to the Euler series on h≥0 suffices via uniqueness of the within-right derivative; full differentiability is not assumed from a one-sided limit.",
